1
00:00:00,033 --> 00:00:03,970
What if I didn't make a big mistake before?

2
00:00:03,970 --> 00:00:05,105
What's going on between you and Liam?

3
00:00:05,105 --> 00:00:06,373
Nothing is going on between us.

4
00:00:06,373 --> 00:00:08,641
I don't know what can happen
because of your choice.

5
00:00:08,641 --> 00:00:10,477
- You're the one I love.
- I finally found you.

6
00:00:10,477 --> 00:00:12,712
Our meeting wasn't an accident.

7
00:00:12,712 --> 00:00:15,081
Every time someone uses this typewriter,

8
00:00:15,081 --> 00:00:19,019
I remember my past, my life story,

9
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:20,520
and the curse of this typewriter.

10
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:24,057
Filipinos see him as a traitor.

11
00:00:24,057 --> 00:00:27,338
And because of the fury
and the desire to be loved...

12
00:00:27,338 --> 00:00:30,930
You will pay for all your sins.

13
00:00:30,930 --> 00:00:33,099
Sabel!

14
00:00:48,782 --> 00:00:50,088
Megan?

15
00:00:50,088 --> 00:00:51,774
Miss Joyce.

16
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:55,205
Megan.

17
00:00:55,205 --> 00:00:58,240
There's something I need to tell you.

18
00:01:09,818 --> 00:01:15,123
The Girl with the Periwinkle Hair...

19
00:01:16,743 --> 00:01:20,379
I manage that account.

20
00:01:22,582 --> 00:01:24,350
Sorry.

21
00:01:25,586 --> 00:01:27,120
That was you?

22
00:01:29,122 --> 00:01:33,459
You are the one who posted
defamatory things about me?

23
00:01:35,496 --> 00:01:37,864
About Liam and me?

24
00:01:44,371 --> 00:01:47,408
Sorry, Miss Joyce.

25
00:01:47,408 --> 00:01:50,743
I needed the money.

26
00:01:52,298 --> 00:01:55,667
I'm the only one who supports my child.

27
00:01:56,608 --> 00:02:00,520
We don't always have projects.

28
00:02:03,090 --> 00:02:07,261
You can slap me or hurt me, Miss Joyce.

29
00:02:07,261 --> 00:02:09,930
If you want to do it, it's okay.

30
00:02:09,930 --> 00:02:15,436
I'm really sorry.
I'm ashamed of what I did.

31
00:02:15,436 --> 00:02:17,937
I'm so sorry, Miss Joyce.

32
00:02:24,508 --> 00:02:27,477
Who's paying you?

33
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:36,022
Who told you to do this?

34
00:02:38,459 --> 00:02:39,995
It's Via.

35
00:02:48,335 --> 00:02:50,737
Miss Joyce, I'm really sorry.

36
00:02:50,737 --> 00:02:52,805
I'm sorry.

37
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:57,543
Please have mercy on me.
My son will be left alone.

38
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:04,083
It hurts to hear this from you, Megan.

39
00:03:08,822 --> 00:03:12,592
I'm hurting because I treat you as family.

40
00:03:18,897 --> 00:03:23,000
I'm not surprised why Via did that to me.

41
00:03:45,097 --> 00:03:48,459
I can only think of one way...

42
00:03:48,459 --> 00:03:51,594
to get Via punished.

43
00:03:58,005 --> 00:04:01,975
You're so cowardly, Hans. So coward!

44
00:04:01,975 --> 00:04:03,943
You're a coward.

45
00:04:07,414 --> 00:04:15,222
You're just a stupid attorney,
who can't even defend himself.

46
00:04:26,066 --> 00:04:28,501
Via, Via.

47
00:04:29,836 --> 00:04:32,272
Let's go home. I'm going home.

48
00:04:32,272 --> 00:04:33,973
Go on.

49
00:04:35,742 --> 00:04:39,246
Everyone leaves me anyway.

50
00:04:44,585 --> 00:04:46,580
Come on. I'll drive you home. Let's go.

51
00:04:46,580 --> 00:04:47,611
No.

52
00:04:47,611 --> 00:04:48,789
Let's go, Via.

53
00:04:48,789 --> 00:04:51,657
- Via!
- I said no!

54
00:05:27,394 --> 00:05:29,129
- Where are you taking me?
- Perverts are not allowed here!

55
00:05:29,129 --> 00:05:30,863
Don't ever come back.

56
00:05:45,245 --> 00:05:46,680
<i>We've arrived in Segunda!</i>

57
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:50,550
<i>This is Lando, my most trusted gunman.</i>

58
00:05:51,184 --> 00:05:52,412
Ouch!

59
00:05:57,024 --> 00:05:58,492
<i>It's nothing.</i>

60
00:05:58,492 --> 00:06:00,427
<i>There's no wound.</i>

61
00:06:00,427 --> 00:06:03,162
<i>What was it that I saw? Did I die?</i>

62
00:06:05,499 --> 00:06:07,834
<i>What's the meaning of that?</i>

63
00:06:07,834 --> 00:06:11,170
<i>What does Liam have to do with all these?</i>

64
00:06:29,957 --> 00:06:32,859
That was deep.

65
00:06:38,498 --> 00:06:41,000
I will turn myself in, Mom.

66
00:06:42,969 --> 00:06:44,504
What?

67
00:06:45,505 --> 00:06:47,173
Why?

68
00:06:48,875 --> 00:06:50,276
Mom...

69
00:06:51,645 --> 00:06:56,616
I need to pay for all the crimes I committed.

70
00:06:57,884 --> 00:06:59,485
And...

71
00:07:00,187 --> 00:07:07,262
this is the only way to stop
Congressman Ramon's evil doings.

72
00:07:07,262 --> 00:07:09,764
Even Lando and...

73
00:07:09,764 --> 00:07:11,299
Vergil.

74
00:07:11,299 --> 00:07:13,634
No matter what happens...

75
00:07:14,269 --> 00:07:21,208
my love for you will never change, my son.

76
00:07:26,681 --> 00:07:28,449
I love you, Mom.

77
00:07:33,154 --> 00:07:34,455
Intoy.

78
00:07:35,823 --> 00:07:38,693
Do you have a place to stay?

79
00:07:38,693 --> 00:07:43,831
You better stay here with the typewriter.

80
00:07:43,831 --> 00:07:47,468
So, at least no one else can use it.

81
00:07:47,468 --> 00:07:50,838
You know how powerful that typewriter is.

82
00:07:50,838 --> 00:07:53,219
We don't know what can happen

83
00:07:53,219 --> 00:07:56,510
if it gets in the hands of the wrong people.

84
00:08:03,518 --> 00:08:05,351
<i>Typewriter...</i>

85
00:08:05,351 --> 00:08:07,355
<i>Powerful?</i>

86
00:08:07,355 --> 00:08:10,124
<i>They seem to have lost it.</i>

87
00:08:13,461 --> 00:08:15,196
<i>Hello, friends!</i>

88
00:08:15,196 --> 00:08:17,899
<i>This is your trusted showbiz authority.</i>

89
00:08:17,899 --> 00:08:21,569
<i>The Girl with the Periwinkle Hair.</i>

90
00:08:21,569 --> 00:08:26,908
<i>But I realized it's also wrong
to hide using a secret identity.</i>

91
00:08:26,908 --> 00:08:30,645
<i>The only thing it does for me
is to escape accountability.</i>

92
00:08:30,645 --> 00:08:34,549
<i>That's why tonight,
I am going to reveal who I really am.</i>

93
00:08:34,549 --> 00:08:37,819
<i>My friends,
The Girl with the Periwinkle hair,</i>

94
00:08:37,819 --> 00:08:42,556
<i>is no other than me, Victoria dela Peña.</i>

95
00:08:58,840 --> 00:09:00,507
Megan!

96
00:09:01,109 --> 00:09:03,611
Megan, get out of there!

97
00:09:03,611 --> 00:09:05,680
What are you posting online?

98
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:07,181
Megan!

99
00:09:07,181 --> 00:09:08,916
Are you looking for Megan?

100
00:09:08,916 --> 00:09:11,619
She left last night with her kid.

101
00:09:11,619 --> 00:09:13,421
They were in a hurry.

102
00:09:13,421 --> 00:09:15,088
She left?

103
00:09:15,690 --> 00:09:17,792
Where did they go?

104
00:09:17,792 --> 00:09:19,760
I don't know.

105
00:09:25,066 --> 00:09:27,135
Isn't that Victoria dela Peña?

106
00:09:27,135 --> 00:09:28,703
That's Via.

107
00:09:28,703 --> 00:09:32,140
The one who confessed she's
The Girl with the Periwinkle Hair.

108
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:35,710
She's the one spreading rumors
about celebrities.

109
00:09:35,710 --> 00:09:37,645
Excuse you.

110
00:09:37,645 --> 00:09:39,447
That's not me.

111
00:09:39,447 --> 00:09:41,449
I don't know what you're talking about.

112
00:09:41,449 --> 00:09:44,085
Where do you think are you going?

113
00:09:44,085 --> 00:09:45,787
- Oh my God!
- Hey, hey!

114
00:09:45,787 --> 00:09:47,346
- What are you doing?
- You deserve this!

115
00:09:47,346 --> 00:09:49,836
Don't touch me!

116
00:09:52,126 --> 00:09:54,394
Get out of here!

117
00:09:56,464 --> 00:09:58,532
Don't ever come back!

118
00:10:10,311 --> 00:10:13,547
We need to talk about Joyce.

119
00:10:18,619 --> 00:10:20,087
Why?

120
00:10:21,022 --> 00:10:22,823
What do you know?

121
00:10:24,692 --> 00:10:26,827
What did Via tell you?

122
00:10:28,029 --> 00:10:30,597
This is not about Via, Hans.

123
00:10:33,167 --> 00:10:35,469
This is about Joyce.

124
00:10:37,338 --> 00:10:42,477
I have to do something important,
and I want you to protect her.

125
00:10:42,477 --> 00:10:44,978
So she won't get involved.

126
00:10:51,252 --> 00:10:52,420
Mr. Herrera,

127
00:10:52,420 --> 00:10:55,590
do you understand that
this is a serious accusation

128
00:10:55,590 --> 00:11:00,127
against the Senate candidate,
Congressman dela Peña?

129
00:11:02,163 --> 00:11:07,702
I'm willing to go to jail
to pay for all my crimes.

130
00:11:07,702 --> 00:11:13,974
I want to make all the culprits pay.

131
00:11:17,678 --> 00:11:18,946
- Sir, question.
- Hold on.

132
00:11:18,946 --> 00:11:21,215
- We're going to start.
- I will just ask questions.

133
00:11:21,215 --> 00:11:24,185
- Sir?
- Go over there for now.

134
00:11:24,185 --> 00:11:25,647
Okay, okay.

135
00:11:31,259 --> 00:11:33,360
Sir, please sit down.

136
00:11:42,537 --> 00:11:46,394
All the money that is being laundered
in Casa Fuerte

137
00:11:46,394 --> 00:11:53,024
comes from the illegal businesses
of Congressman Ramon dela Peña,

138
00:11:53,024 --> 00:11:56,110
under my authorization.

139
00:11:56,984 --> 00:12:03,824
We also collect dirty money
from different parts of the country.

140
00:12:03,824 --> 00:12:07,939
We invest it in Casa Fuerte to launder it.

141
00:12:07,939 --> 00:12:12,567
I run the company as CEO.

142
00:12:12,567 --> 00:12:17,370
And the president of the company,
your father, Danilo Herrera?

143
00:12:17,370 --> 00:12:19,774
He doesn't know anything about this.
[Seal of the President of the Philippines]

144
00:12:19,774 --> 00:12:24,312
Mr. President,
Congressman Ramon dela Peña is here.

145
00:12:24,312 --> 00:12:26,055
Let him in.

146
00:12:32,954 --> 00:12:36,067
<i>My half-brother Vergil Herrera</i>

147
00:12:36,067 --> 00:12:40,132
<i>took over my position in Casa Fuerte.</i>

148
00:12:41,529 --> 00:12:45,600
Mr. President,
I thought this is an intimate meeting.

149
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:49,011
<i>He also knows</i>

150
00:12:49,011 --> 00:12:52,607
all the illegal dealings
of Congressman Ramon,

151
00:12:52,607 --> 00:12:55,493
which were executed
by his right-hand man, Lando.

152
00:12:55,493 --> 00:12:57,117
Lando Nakpil.

153
00:13:00,179 --> 00:13:02,116
- <i>We also collect...</i>
- Go on.

154
00:13:02,116 --> 00:13:03,317
Leave us alone for now.

155
00:13:03,317 --> 00:13:07,121
<i>That comes from different parts
of the country.</i>

156
00:13:07,121 --> 00:13:11,228
<i>Then, we invest it in Casa Fuerte
to launder it.</i>

157
00:13:11,228 --> 00:13:17,331
Mr. President, I assure you that he's lying.

158
00:13:17,331 --> 00:13:21,530
That Liam Herrera is from my rival's camp.

159
00:13:22,903 --> 00:13:24,905
Who's the rival you're referring to,
Congressman dela Peña?

160
00:13:24,905 --> 00:13:28,175
Those that I defeated in my district
who wanted to smear my reputation

161
00:13:28,175 --> 00:13:32,846
because I'm doing well
in the senatorial surveys.

162
00:13:35,284 --> 00:13:40,989
The House Ethics Committee
is set to open an investigation.

163
00:13:40,989 --> 00:13:43,392
Ethics Committee?

164
00:13:43,392 --> 00:13:45,394
Wait, Mr. Speaker.

165
00:13:45,394 --> 00:13:49,998
Did you check if Liam is telling the truth?

166
00:13:49,998 --> 00:13:51,733
Mr. President, are you going to believe...

167
00:13:51,733 --> 00:13:53,832
Stop it, Ramon!

168
00:13:56,238 --> 00:14:01,376
I believe that you serve
the people with honesty.

169
00:14:03,245 --> 00:14:07,916
I also believe that you are
popular among the masses,

170
00:14:07,916 --> 00:14:11,437
that's why you were included
in the senatorial slate.

171
00:14:12,254 --> 00:14:18,319
But it turns out,
you are one who can bring the party down.

172
00:14:19,219 --> 00:14:22,431
Mr. President, hear me out.

173
00:14:22,431 --> 00:14:24,766
Let the court decide.

174
00:14:24,766 --> 00:14:27,669
Ramon, listen carefully.

175
00:14:27,669 --> 00:14:31,974
Once all the accusations against you
are proven to be true,

176
00:14:31,974 --> 00:14:35,007
I will make sure you'll go to jail.

177
00:14:36,111 --> 00:14:39,147
Ramon, I also regret to inform you

178
00:14:39,147 --> 00:14:41,683
that you're no longer a member of the party.

179
00:14:41,683 --> 00:14:46,688
You can still pursue
your senatorial aspiration,

180
00:14:46,688 --> 00:14:51,479
but you can't get any endorsement or support
from the party

181
00:14:51,479 --> 00:14:53,974
or the President.

182
00:14:59,635 --> 00:15:02,107
You'll regret this.

183
00:15:19,554 --> 00:15:21,119
Stop!

184
00:15:25,927 --> 00:15:27,463
This way!

185
00:15:28,864 --> 00:15:31,970
Liam is such a pest. He's a troublemaker.

186
00:16:03,398 --> 00:16:05,027
Dad.

187
00:16:13,742 --> 00:16:15,264
Dad.

188
00:16:16,378 --> 00:16:18,217
I need your help.

189
00:16:22,117 --> 00:16:23,551
Help?

190
00:16:25,921 --> 00:16:29,045
What is it, my dear daughter?

191
00:16:38,066 --> 00:16:43,113
Megan has exposed me
as The Girl with the Periwinkle Hair.

192
00:16:43,939 --> 00:16:45,841
They're talking about me online.

193
00:16:45,841 --> 00:16:47,609
People are talking too much.

194
00:16:47,609 --> 00:16:50,199
They're already ruining my image.

195
00:16:53,148 --> 00:16:55,191
Isn't it true?

196
00:17:02,424 --> 00:17:09,797
Do you think I still
have time to worry about you?

197
00:17:12,701 --> 00:17:16,308
Do you know what happened earlier?

198
00:17:20,108 --> 00:17:26,248
The President of the Philippines
kicked me out of the party!

199
00:17:28,950 --> 00:17:32,287
My political career is ruined.

200
00:17:32,287 --> 00:17:39,100
And you want me to solve
that worthless Periwinkle thing?

201
00:17:43,965 --> 00:17:48,370
Your boyfriend, Liam,
has caused my downfall.

202
00:17:48,370 --> 00:17:55,310
You brought that bad luck to our family, Via.

203
00:17:55,310 --> 00:17:59,514
He has too many exposés about me.

204
00:17:59,514 --> 00:18:01,183
Why?

205
00:18:01,183 --> 00:18:03,318
Isn't it true?

206
00:18:03,318 --> 00:18:04,820
Darn it!

207
00:18:04,820 --> 00:18:07,601
Don't use my words against me!

208
00:18:09,758 --> 00:18:12,116
Just admit it, Dad.

209
00:18:13,829 --> 00:18:18,960
We both have rotten personalities.

210
00:18:22,704 --> 00:18:27,278
You pretend to be a good person
in front of others.

211
00:18:28,510 --> 00:18:33,458
If I'm plastic, then you're rubber.

212
00:18:35,417 --> 00:18:38,247
We're both going to burn in hell.

213
00:18:42,656 --> 00:18:44,771
But you are worse than I am.

214
00:18:47,529 --> 00:18:48,730
That's enough.

215
00:18:48,730 --> 00:18:50,932
Go ahead!

216
00:18:50,932 --> 00:18:53,711
I'm already numb, Dad.

217
00:18:55,666 --> 00:18:58,601
You've killed me long ago.

218
00:19:16,057 --> 00:19:18,435
- Hans.
- Aunt Tess.

219
00:19:23,999 --> 00:19:26,380
What does this mean?

220
00:19:27,469 --> 00:19:29,604
You have to come with us.

221
00:19:29,604 --> 00:19:33,796
Liam asked me to take you to a safe house.

222
00:19:36,144 --> 00:19:38,246
Intoy isn't here yet.

223
00:19:38,246 --> 00:19:40,421
Who's Intoy?

224
00:19:42,584 --> 00:19:46,021
He's the man staying with us.

225
00:19:46,021 --> 00:19:50,850
I'm sorry, Aunt Tess. We need to leave now.

226
00:19:52,594 --> 00:19:57,732
Do we really need to hide from Ramon
like we are rats?

227
00:19:58,931 --> 00:20:04,306
He will not stop until he gets back at Liam

228
00:20:04,306 --> 00:20:07,675
and at everyone dear to him,
while he's still in power.

229
00:20:10,512 --> 00:20:11,780
Okay.

230
00:20:11,780 --> 00:20:14,482
But please come back for Intoy, okay?

231
00:20:14,482 --> 00:20:16,101
We will.

232
00:20:20,455 --> 00:20:22,290
Borj, thank you.

233
00:20:22,290 --> 00:20:24,421
You even brought me food.

234
00:20:25,660 --> 00:20:27,629
It's nothing, Boss Bro.

235
00:20:27,629 --> 00:20:29,280
Anything for you.

236
00:20:30,732 --> 00:20:34,161
Deedee and Leroy want to say hi to you.

237
00:20:35,403 --> 00:20:39,441
They got a new project
in a rising film company.

238
00:20:45,480 --> 00:20:47,649
Why are you so quiet?

239
00:20:47,649 --> 00:20:50,069
I'm not used to seeing you like that.

240
00:20:51,419 --> 00:20:53,314
Nothing, Boss Bro.

241
00:20:54,990 --> 00:20:57,492
I'm just shocked at what happened.

242
00:20:57,492 --> 00:21:00,942
I feel like I didn't give my all.

243
00:21:02,728 --> 00:21:05,299
I've been your assistant for years,

244
00:21:05,299 --> 00:21:08,169
but I learned only now
about your dirty business.

245
00:21:08,169 --> 00:21:13,675
If I only knew, I could have stopped you.

246
00:21:13,675 --> 00:21:18,069
Borj, you did nothing wrong.

247
00:21:23,084 --> 00:21:24,819
Thank you.

248
00:21:26,688 --> 00:21:28,423
Thank you so much, Borj.

249
00:21:28,423 --> 00:21:31,126
Boss Bro, you sound like...

250
00:21:31,126 --> 00:21:33,128
you're saying goodbye.

251
00:21:33,128 --> 00:21:35,764
I'm just going on a vacation.

252
00:21:35,764 --> 00:21:38,938
But I think it's going to be a long one.

253
00:21:40,301 --> 00:21:47,776
Seriously, Borj, thank you for your loyalty.

254
00:21:47,776 --> 00:21:52,436
Thank you for the friendship.

255
00:21:55,216 --> 00:21:57,827
Promise me, Borj...

256
00:22:00,922 --> 00:22:04,167
that no matter what happens,

257
00:22:04,167 --> 00:22:06,628
you won't end up like me.

258
00:22:06,628 --> 00:22:08,897
Work decently.

259
00:22:08,897 --> 00:22:10,358
Boss Bro.

260
00:22:11,566 --> 00:22:14,028
I should thank you.

261
00:22:15,904 --> 00:22:18,450
Thank you for...

262
00:22:19,974 --> 00:22:21,989
trusting me.

263
00:22:24,846 --> 00:22:29,788
Borj, always take care.

264
00:22:31,019 --> 00:22:34,272
I'm worried that you will get involved too,

265
00:22:34,272 --> 00:22:36,790
given Congressman Ramon's temper.

266
00:22:39,828 --> 00:22:40,829
Don't worry about me.

267
00:22:40,829 --> 00:22:43,259
I can take care of myself, Boss Bro.

268
00:22:45,266 --> 00:22:47,368
Go on and eat.

269
00:22:47,368 --> 00:22:48,937
What's this?

270
00:22:48,937 --> 00:22:49,938
Betute.

271
00:22:49,938 --> 00:22:51,633
Wow.

272
00:22:52,656 --> 00:22:54,843
Liam has listed your name
for the protection program

273
00:22:54,843 --> 00:23:00,992
to keep you safe
from the people he will identify.

274
00:23:03,785 --> 00:23:06,287
How long do we stay here
in the safe house, Ma'am?

275
00:23:06,287 --> 00:23:09,224
There's no definite time.

276
00:23:09,224 --> 00:23:13,257
But you have to stay here
until the situation settles down.

277
00:23:14,329 --> 00:23:16,698
Madam policewoman, thank you.

278
00:23:16,698 --> 00:23:21,280
I don't want to die young
because I still want to get married.

279
00:23:23,238 --> 00:23:25,640
Hello, Jana.

280
00:23:25,640 --> 00:23:27,842
Do you know what's the latest?

281
00:23:27,842 --> 00:23:32,680
My goodness! Via and his father,
Congressman Ramon,

282
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:36,151
they are spreading evil!

283
00:23:36,151 --> 00:23:37,719
Jana, you know what to do.

284
00:23:37,719 --> 00:23:41,055
Make this issue explosive.

285
00:23:41,055 --> 00:23:43,825
Ruin Via.

286
00:23:43,825 --> 00:23:49,989
She has no one to take after
than her darn father.

287
00:23:50,932 --> 00:23:53,001
Okay. Very good.

288
00:23:53,001 --> 00:23:54,395
Do it.

289
00:23:55,737 --> 00:23:57,338
You didn't forget about me.

290
00:23:57,338 --> 00:23:58,840
Ginataang betute.

291
00:23:58,840 --> 00:24:00,341
This is good!

292
00:24:00,341 --> 00:24:01,700
Liam.

293
00:24:02,649 --> 00:24:04,099
Sir.

294
00:24:12,020 --> 00:24:13,489
Dad.

295
00:24:23,198 --> 00:24:25,400
Dad, I'm sorry.

296
00:24:25,400 --> 00:24:27,902
- No...
- I'm sorry.

297
00:24:27,902 --> 00:24:30,605
I should apologize to you.

298
00:24:30,605 --> 00:24:33,541
I have a lot of shortcomings.

299
00:24:33,541 --> 00:24:35,867
I turned a blind eye on Ramon.

300
00:24:51,326 --> 00:24:52,649
Dad.

301
00:24:53,895 --> 00:24:56,831
Dad, you did nothing wrong.

302
00:24:56,831 --> 00:24:59,667
This all started with me.
Vergil just continued it.

303
00:24:59,667 --> 00:25:01,102
But you...

304
00:25:01,102 --> 00:25:03,430
you're innocent.

305
00:25:05,473 --> 00:25:08,009
This is your fault, Liam.

306
00:25:08,009 --> 00:25:09,777
You're inconsiderate.

307
00:25:09,777 --> 00:25:12,447
If you want to go to jail, just do so!

308
00:25:12,447 --> 00:25:16,017
- Why did you have to get me involved?
- You did worse than me, Vergil.

309
00:25:16,017 --> 00:25:19,921
You think I don't know
you were at the orphanage when Sep died?

310
00:25:19,921 --> 00:25:23,124
- Watch your...
- Shut up!

311
00:25:23,124 --> 00:25:25,426
The kid asked you for help
when he was having a heart attack.

312
00:25:25,426 --> 00:25:27,328
But what did you do?

313
00:25:27,328 --> 00:25:30,763
You walked away
like you didn't see or hear anything!

314
00:25:30,763 --> 00:25:32,033
You, monster!

315
00:25:32,033 --> 00:25:34,202
You let an innocent kid die!

316
00:25:34,202 --> 00:25:35,918
Take back what you said!

317
00:25:36,771 --> 00:25:38,699
- That's enough!
- Stop!

318
00:25:39,774 --> 00:25:40,808
Is that true?

319
00:25:40,808 --> 00:25:41,776
Is that true?

320
00:25:41,776 --> 00:25:42,944
Dad...

321
00:25:42,944 --> 00:25:44,779
That's enough!

322
00:25:44,779 --> 00:25:45,947
Stop it! You can't make a scene here!

323
00:25:45,947 --> 00:25:47,682
You're evil!

324
00:25:47,682 --> 00:25:50,066
I raised a demon!

325
00:25:51,152 --> 00:25:53,688
Stop! You can't cause trouble here!

326
00:25:53,688 --> 00:25:56,012
Put them back in the cell.

327
00:26:16,377 --> 00:26:19,213
I thought this place was safe.

328
00:26:19,213 --> 00:26:23,618
But there is someone here
who's making it otherwise.

329
00:26:23,618 --> 00:26:26,613
Is there a problem, Joanne?

330
00:26:26,613 --> 00:26:29,123
Yes, a big problem.

331
00:26:29,123 --> 00:26:32,993
Because all along,
my suspicions about your son were right.

332
00:26:32,993 --> 00:26:34,428
Bad news.

333
00:26:34,428 --> 00:26:37,164
He can't be trusted.

334
00:26:37,164 --> 00:26:40,100
What do we care about your family's mess?

335
00:26:40,100 --> 00:26:43,503
I didn't do anything wrong
to Congressman Ramon!

336
00:26:43,503 --> 00:26:46,714
My son is just doing the right thing.

337
00:26:47,541 --> 00:26:49,943
No one is forcing you to stay
if you don't want to be here.

338
00:26:49,943 --> 00:26:51,411
You can leave if you want.

339
00:26:51,411 --> 00:26:52,846
Yes. I'm leaving.

340
00:26:52,846 --> 00:26:55,064
That's enough, Joanne!

341
00:26:56,883 --> 00:26:59,619
I don't care about your son's crimes!

342
00:26:59,619 --> 00:27:05,058
What I hate the most is
being bothered by someone else's mess!

343
00:27:05,058 --> 00:27:08,599
I can afford my own security.

344
00:27:09,463 --> 00:27:12,098
Odet, Joyce, let's go.

345
00:27:12,098 --> 00:27:14,034
Oh, Madam! Madam!

346
00:27:14,034 --> 00:27:16,203
What about my private security?

347
00:27:16,203 --> 00:27:18,088
I don't want to get kidnapped.

348
00:27:18,770 --> 00:27:21,166
Do you think someone
will take interest in you?

349
00:27:21,166 --> 00:27:23,076
Excuse me.

350
00:27:23,076 --> 00:27:26,279
Mom, let's be reasonable.

351
00:27:26,279 --> 00:27:28,048
Joyce is right, Aunt Joanne.

352
00:27:28,048 --> 00:27:31,117
We don't know what can happen.

353
00:27:31,117 --> 00:27:34,888
This safe house is too small for Tess and me.

354
00:27:34,888 --> 00:27:36,423
Okay, let's do this.

355
00:27:36,423 --> 00:27:39,593
I will let you go back to your house.

356
00:27:39,593 --> 00:27:42,596
But you will be under police surveillance

357
00:27:42,596 --> 00:27:46,733
until you get your own security detail.

358
00:27:46,733 --> 00:27:49,402
I'm telling you...

359
00:27:49,402 --> 00:27:51,888
it's dangerous to stay in your house.

360
00:27:52,772 --> 00:27:55,775
Okay, fine.

361
00:27:55,775 --> 00:27:57,411
Where's my room?

362
00:27:59,112 --> 00:28:00,413
Let's go.

363
00:28:00,413 --> 00:28:02,749
See? She's scared.

364
00:28:02,749 --> 00:28:03,683
What did you say?

365
00:28:03,683 --> 00:28:04,684
- Oh, nothing.
- Let's go!

366
00:28:04,684 --> 00:28:06,774
I said, let's go.

367
00:28:14,828 --> 00:28:16,630
Tess?

368
00:28:16,630 --> 00:28:18,319
Liam?

369
00:28:37,017 --> 00:28:38,969
The typewriter!

370
00:29:13,720 --> 00:29:15,210
Via.

371
00:29:22,529 --> 00:29:24,580
How could you?

372
00:29:27,033 --> 00:29:30,943
After everything that my dad did for you.

373
00:29:33,773 --> 00:29:35,669
Via, I'm sorry.

374
00:29:38,178 --> 00:29:40,874
But maybe it's time...

375
00:29:42,415 --> 00:29:44,676
to do what's right.

376
00:29:46,386 --> 00:29:48,020
Do what's right?

377
00:29:50,190 --> 00:29:55,606
Is it right to betray
your girlfriend's father?

378
00:29:59,699 --> 00:30:02,469
We have to stop this.

379
00:30:02,469 --> 00:30:03,741
What?

380
00:30:04,537 --> 00:30:06,616
Via, I tried.

381
00:30:09,542 --> 00:30:13,580
I tried to love you. Believe me.

382
00:30:13,580 --> 00:30:15,389
Tried?

383
00:30:16,416 --> 00:30:18,537
Tell me the truth.

384
00:30:23,590 --> 00:30:26,139
Did you really love me?

385
00:30:30,296 --> 00:30:36,818
I know how much you loved me.

386
00:30:40,740 --> 00:30:42,909
And I will never forget that.

387
00:30:42,909 --> 00:30:45,119
So I'm sorry, Via.

388
00:30:55,689 --> 00:30:57,555
Sorry?

389
00:30:58,491 --> 00:31:00,260
You are sorry, Liam? That's all I get?

390
00:31:00,260 --> 00:31:01,977
An apology?

391
00:31:30,023 --> 00:31:35,363
There's a special place in hell
for the both of you.

392
00:31:38,398 --> 00:31:40,213
You deserve to be together.

393
00:31:58,361 --> 00:32:00,220
Do you think I will see you differently

394
00:32:00,220 --> 00:32:03,892
just because you owned up to your mistakes?

395
00:32:05,592 --> 00:32:08,978
Whether you see me differently or not,
Joyce...

396
00:32:10,830 --> 00:32:12,931
it doesn't matter.

397
00:32:15,034 --> 00:32:17,091
I just...

398
00:32:18,505 --> 00:32:22,375
want to rectify all my mistakes.

399
00:32:22,375 --> 00:32:26,446
I don't want anyone else to suffer
because of my wrong decisions.

400
00:32:26,446 --> 00:32:30,092
I wish you have thought
about that before, Liam.

401
00:32:31,618 --> 00:32:36,228
You should have thought about it
before you ruined my life.

402
00:32:40,026 --> 00:32:43,263
Turning yourself in won't fix
all the trouble you caused.

403
00:32:43,263 --> 00:32:45,298
Remember that.

404
00:32:45,298 --> 00:32:48,802
You're no different from
Ramon dela Peña, Vergil, Via...

405
00:32:48,802 --> 00:32:50,069
You are all the same!

406
00:32:50,069 --> 00:32:51,938
You all ruined my life!

407
00:32:51,938 --> 00:32:53,306
You are no different from them.

408
00:32:53,306 --> 00:32:55,108
You all killed Sep!

409
00:32:55,108 --> 00:32:57,811
- You made my father blind!
- Joyce...

410
00:32:57,811 --> 00:32:59,145
I was just a puppet at Casa Fuerte.

411
00:32:59,145 --> 00:33:00,980
I had nothing to do
with Uncle Edmond's blindness

412
00:33:00,980 --> 00:33:02,916
nor with Sep's death.

413
00:33:02,916 --> 00:33:05,652
The only wrong I did
was I used the typewriter.

414
00:33:05,652 --> 00:33:08,911
Stop it! Enough, please. Stop!

415
00:33:14,541 --> 00:33:16,062
Don't blame the typewriter.

416
00:33:16,062 --> 00:33:20,267
Don't blame all your mistakes on a fantasy.

417
00:33:24,504 --> 00:33:27,307
If it's true that these
are all the typewriter's fault,

418
00:33:27,307 --> 00:33:28,930
you shouldn't have...

419
00:33:30,810 --> 00:33:32,812
You shouldn't have
brought me back to life!

420
00:33:32,812 --> 00:33:35,535
You should have just let me die!

421
00:33:40,820 --> 00:33:42,989
I will ask again.

422
00:33:42,989 --> 00:33:48,928
What secret does the typewriter have?

423
00:33:48,928 --> 00:33:50,947
What?

424
00:33:53,633 --> 00:33:56,002
You can do everything you want with me.

425
00:33:56,002 --> 00:33:57,437
You can kill me if you want!

426
00:33:57,437 --> 00:33:59,413
But I will never die!

427
00:34:05,778 --> 00:34:14,354
You may not die,
but that doesn't mean you don't get hurt.

428
00:34:14,354 --> 00:34:17,056
So? Does it hurt?

429
00:34:17,056 --> 00:34:19,392
Does it hurt?

430
00:34:22,395 --> 00:34:25,064
With that look right now,

431
00:34:25,064 --> 00:34:28,201
you just might wish
that you are not immortal...

432
00:34:28,201 --> 00:34:30,236
That you'd rather die!

433
00:34:30,236 --> 00:34:32,049
Is that right?

434
00:34:54,394 --> 00:34:57,031
What did you and Liam talk about?

435
00:34:58,864 --> 00:35:01,099
I have no obligation to tell you.

436
00:35:01,099 --> 00:35:03,227
Let me get it straight.

437
00:35:04,136 --> 00:35:06,294
Are you mad at me because

438
00:35:06,294 --> 00:35:10,742
you found out that I'm the person
behind The Girl with the Periwinkle Hair?

439
00:35:12,044 --> 00:35:13,636
Why, though?

440
00:35:14,713 --> 00:35:17,738
Everything I said was true, anyway.

441
00:35:18,717 --> 00:35:21,964
Even the thing about your junkie father.

442
00:35:30,695 --> 00:35:32,983
It's all true, Joyce.

443
00:35:36,068 --> 00:35:38,804
All the secrets I revealed...

444
00:35:38,804 --> 00:35:41,073
you had it coming your way.

445
00:35:41,073 --> 00:35:44,397
You and your whole family!

446
00:35:47,245 --> 00:35:49,848
Remember this, Joyce.

447
00:35:49,848 --> 00:35:51,983
No secret remains hidden.

448
00:35:51,983 --> 00:35:54,086
How?

449
00:35:54,086 --> 00:35:57,244
How can I make you pay?

450
00:36:00,200 --> 00:36:02,830
For making my father blind?

451
00:36:04,663 --> 00:36:07,015
Who told you that, Joyce?

452
00:36:09,267 --> 00:36:11,024
Was it Liam?

453
00:36:12,270 --> 00:36:14,588
Who told you that?

454
00:36:18,110 --> 00:36:20,791
You said so yourself.

455
00:36:23,882 --> 00:36:27,010
No secret remains hidden.

456
00:36:28,920 --> 00:36:32,478
Be prepared to pay for all your sins.

457
00:36:57,115 --> 00:37:03,321
How does the darn typewriter work?

458
00:37:03,321 --> 00:37:06,624
I won't tell you anything!

459
00:37:07,626 --> 00:37:10,328
You're stubborn.

460
00:37:10,328 --> 00:37:18,336
If you're not worth anything,
I should kill Liam instead.

461
00:37:18,336 --> 00:37:22,908
Or Tess...

462
00:37:22,908 --> 00:37:24,342
Don't.

463
00:37:24,342 --> 00:37:26,244
Don't!

464
00:37:26,244 --> 00:37:28,113
Don't do that! Don't!

465
00:37:33,018 --> 00:37:34,621
Fine.

466
00:37:35,854 --> 00:37:39,108
You can change past events...

467
00:37:40,091 --> 00:37:42,569
Past events in your life...

468
00:37:43,528 --> 00:37:46,288
If you rewrite it using the typewriter.

469
00:37:55,307 --> 00:37:56,937
It's like a genie...

470
00:37:59,000 --> 00:38:00,612
Right, like a genie.

471
00:38:00,612 --> 00:38:01,947
That's it?

472
00:38:01,947 --> 00:38:04,783
Nothing more? Is that it?

473
00:38:04,783 --> 00:38:06,618
You animal!

474
00:38:06,618 --> 00:38:11,125
Why didn't I realize this soon?

475
00:38:11,125 --> 00:38:13,558
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

476
00:38:14,793 --> 00:38:22,400
That's why I feel like I died
but came back to life.

477
00:38:25,470 --> 00:38:27,138
You should die!

478
00:38:27,138 --> 00:38:31,488
The typewriter can bring
the dead back to life?

479
00:38:33,178 --> 00:38:34,738
Wow.

480
00:38:44,522 --> 00:38:47,609
You monster! Don't take it away!

481
00:39:09,547 --> 00:39:13,218
You're the one who brought tragedy
into this family.

482
00:39:13,218 --> 00:39:15,900
It happens again and again.

483
00:39:19,391 --> 00:39:25,223
And it all started...
when you cheated on mom.

484
00:39:28,211 --> 00:39:30,020
You had an affair.

485
00:39:33,972 --> 00:39:36,451
I made a mistake.

486
00:39:37,876 --> 00:39:41,623
But she didn't give me a second chance.

487
00:39:43,214 --> 00:39:48,678
I begged her, but... she won't hear me out.

488
00:39:49,654 --> 00:39:51,819
So from then on,

489
00:39:54,086 --> 00:39:57,999
I hate begging for second chances.

490
00:40:00,598 --> 00:40:02,822
So it is true.

491
00:40:06,143 --> 00:40:08,969
Mom took her own life...

492
00:40:11,385 --> 00:40:13,265
because of you.

493
00:40:16,314 --> 00:40:20,919
I lost my mom because of you.

494
00:40:20,919 --> 00:40:23,630
When Mom died,

495
00:40:26,157 --> 00:40:33,048
I thought, finally,
since it's just the two of us,

496
00:40:33,048 --> 00:40:35,414
I would feel your presence.

497
00:40:37,769 --> 00:40:39,969
But I was wrong.

498
00:40:42,774 --> 00:40:46,141
You know what hurts me, Dad?

499
00:40:48,813 --> 00:40:54,232
I wasn't enough reason for you to fight...

500
00:40:58,289 --> 00:41:03,444
and strive to become a good person
because you still have a child.

501
00:41:05,296 --> 00:41:07,093
What for?

502
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:10,558
Who are you?

503
00:41:11,803 --> 00:41:13,503
Are you her?

504
00:41:14,506 --> 00:41:16,972
Did I do you wrong?

505
00:41:17,976 --> 00:41:20,167
You're just my child.

506
00:41:23,815 --> 00:41:27,852
I won't change just for you.

507
00:41:27,852 --> 00:41:33,595
You have nothing else in your mind
aside from your obsession with Liam.

508
00:41:37,896 --> 00:41:42,100
If there's something
I'll ask for forgiveness,

509
00:41:42,100 --> 00:41:45,937
it will be what's going to happen tonight.

510
00:41:45,937 --> 00:41:49,306
Because I will kill Liam.

511
00:41:50,575 --> 00:41:52,177
No, Dad.

512
00:41:52,177 --> 00:41:54,112
No. No, Dad, no!

513
00:41:54,112 --> 00:41:55,680
No, don't do that, please!

514
00:41:55,680 --> 00:41:59,617
- Take it back! That's not true!
- Get off me!

515
00:41:59,617 --> 00:42:02,253
Dad, don't, please! Please. Dad...

516
00:42:02,253 --> 00:42:04,022
Not Liam, please.

517
00:42:04,022 --> 00:42:05,924
Dad, not Liam!

518
00:42:05,924 --> 00:42:08,335
Dad!

519
00:42:17,068 --> 00:42:19,663
I need your help right now.

520
00:42:21,072 --> 00:42:22,941
Hey, where are you taking me?

521
00:42:22,941 --> 00:42:24,642
Just chill, kid.

522
00:42:24,642 --> 00:42:27,210
Your outfit suits the event tonight.

523
00:42:31,049 --> 00:42:32,572
Take him.

524
00:42:38,050 --> 00:42:41,259
Hans, I want to ask your forgiveness...

525
00:42:42,627 --> 00:42:46,856
For all the time that I made you wait.

526
00:42:47,989 --> 00:42:51,536
Now, you're still here...

527
00:42:53,137 --> 00:42:56,994
You're still waiting for me. I'm sorry.

528
00:42:58,977 --> 00:43:00,705
Maybe...

529
00:43:03,314 --> 00:43:07,737
like in the films...

530
00:43:09,454 --> 00:43:13,316
We're not meant to be together in the end.

531
00:43:23,001 --> 00:43:26,337
I'll cherish everything that we shared.

532
00:43:26,337 --> 00:43:29,841
You're such a good person.

533
00:43:29,841 --> 00:43:34,661
I want to choose you, but...

534
00:43:35,813 --> 00:43:38,716
You don't have to force yourself.

535
00:43:39,984 --> 00:43:45,356
What's in your heart is all that matters.

536
00:43:45,356 --> 00:43:49,294
Don't worry if you're
going to hurt other people.

537
00:43:49,294 --> 00:43:52,105
Joyce, what's important is for you
to be happy.

538
00:43:53,364 --> 00:43:56,144
I'll be okay with that.

539
00:43:58,469 --> 00:44:04,642
I don't want you to regret
your decision someday.

540
00:44:04,642 --> 00:44:06,555
I don't want that.

541
00:44:13,691 --> 00:44:15,872
[Ms. Joyce, you instructed me
to keep an eye on Mr. Herrera.]

542
00:44:15,872 --> 00:44:18,000
[He was brought to this address:
Pulang Buhangin]

543
00:44:27,552 --> 00:44:30,031
I'm glad you came.

544
00:44:36,018 --> 00:44:37,711
What's that?

545
00:44:44,515 --> 00:44:47,708
Long story.

546
00:44:48,586 --> 00:44:50,188
Come with me.

547
00:44:50,188 --> 00:44:52,256
Dad will kill Liam.

548
00:44:52,256 --> 00:44:54,416
Where can they possibly go?

549
00:44:55,860 --> 00:44:57,929
I'll stay out of that, Via.

550
00:44:57,929 --> 00:45:01,270
That's between you and your dad.

551
00:45:02,153 --> 00:45:04,012
Are you serious?

552
00:45:06,270 --> 00:45:07,957
How much?

553
00:45:15,434 --> 00:45:17,340
I'm sorry.

554
00:45:20,118 --> 00:45:22,543
Thank you so much...

555
00:45:23,725 --> 00:45:25,855
for everything.

556
00:45:28,393 --> 00:45:31,957
You deserve to be happy.

557
00:45:35,967 --> 00:45:39,371
You should be free.

558
00:46:05,129 --> 00:46:10,957
<i>Maybe in this lifetime,
we're not meant for each other.</i>

559
00:46:21,994 --> 00:46:23,014
Dad!

560
00:46:23,014 --> 00:46:25,750
I won't let Dad kill you.

561
00:46:25,750 --> 00:46:27,719
We'll be together. This is what I want.

562
00:46:27,719 --> 00:46:29,020
This is my wish.

563
00:46:29,020 --> 00:46:30,855
Dex!

564
00:46:30,855 --> 00:46:33,591
- Joyce.
- Liam is my husband.

565
00:46:33,591 --> 00:46:35,393
Liam and Via suddenly disappeared.

566
00:46:35,393 --> 00:46:36,794
They're looking for them now.

567
00:46:36,794 --> 00:46:37,962
What?

568
00:46:37,962 --> 00:46:40,732
I was badly injured because of the gunshot.

569
00:46:40,732 --> 00:46:43,267
Why did you take the bullet for me?

570
00:46:43,267 --> 00:46:44,681
I don't know, either.

571
00:46:44,681 --> 00:46:47,898
All I know is, I love you.

572
00:46:49,376 --> 00:46:50,890
Mom.
